    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d181">

                <pb facs="0262" n="196" sameAs="frus:frus1934v05/pg196"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">839.51/4105: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in the Dominican Republic</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Schoenfeld</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Santo
                                Domingo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1934-04-21T15:00:00-05:00">April 21, 1934—3
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 7:42 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>10. See my despatch No. 1529, April 4.<anchor n="12" xml:id="d181-f1"/> My
                    despatch No. 1553 today<anchor n="12" xml:id="d181-f2"/> which goes forward by
                    airmail April 23 reports information, unofficial but believed authentic, that
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">a</hi>) determined efforts have lately been made by
                    the Dominican Government to enlist cooperation of American sugar interests
                    operating in this country in endeavoring to expedite Dominican debt negotiations
                    in the United States by giving companies assurance that proposed levy of export
                    tax on sugar will not be effective if they will so cooperate; (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">b</hi>) that Mr. E. I. Kilbourne of West Indies Sugar
                    Company left this morning for the United States by air to urge agreement as to
                    Dominican debt service on basis desired by Dominican Government; and that (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">c</hi>) the President of the Republic would consider
                    favorably suggestion by the Department <pb facs="0263" n="197" xml:id="pg197"/>
                    or by Foreign Bondholders Protective Council that expert be sent here to
                    investigate financial and fiscal condition of Dominican Government, though the
                    President feels he cannot make this suggestion himself.</p>
                <p>See also last sentence, page 6, my despatch 1263, November 4, 1933.<anchor n="13"
                        xml:id="d181-f3"/></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Schoenfeld</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
